CAREBRIDGE

A simple healthcare-focused web app that brings a few useful things together in one place.
Live: https://quiz-java-q40o7kuko-suryanshyadavyt-crypto.vercel.app/

What is CareBridge?

The idea behind CareBridge was pretty simple: if someone isn't feeling well, they shouldn't have to jump between different websites just to find basic information or a nearby hospital.
So I built a small web app that combines:
- Health guidance for some common problems
- Nearby hospitals and healthcare facilities
- An interactive map
- A basic wellbeing check-in
- A personal health card for important information

FEATURES

Health Guidance

Select a common health problem and get some basic information and things you can consider doing.
Find Nearby Hospitals
With location permission, CareBridge finds nearby healthcare facilities and shows them on a map.
The map uses Leaflet, while healthcare locations are fetched using OpenStreetMap / Overpass API.

Health Card

A small personal card where you can save things like:
- Name
- Blood group
- Emergency contact
- Notes

The information is currently saved in the browser using LocalStorage.
Wellbeing Check-in

A simple way to record how you're feeling and keep track of your check-ins.

Tech Used
- HTML
- CSS
- JavaScript
- React
- Vite
- Leaflet
- OpenStreetMap
- Overpass API
- LocalStorage

Running it locally

Clone the repository:

git clone https://github.com/suryanshyadavyt-crypto/carebridge.git
cd carebridge

Install the dependencies:

npm install
Run the development server:
npm run dev
Then open the local URL shown by Vite.

